    "body": "I guess `2> $null` is PowerShell's way of doing `2>/dev/null` right?\r\n\r\nStarship will try to execute your command by spawning subshell from the current parent `SHELL` ie PowerShell with `cmd.exe` used as a fallback. I guess what is happening here is that your command and when clause for some reason gets interpreted by `cmd.exe` fallback instead which choked on `$null` part thus always returning non-zero exit code.\r\nTry setting `shell` option explicitly to `pwsh` or remove that error redirection because `when` output won't get printed anyway.",
