    "body": "> I guess `2> $null` is PowerShell's way of doing `2>/dev/null` right?\r\n\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n> Also, you can set STARSHIP_LOG environment variable to trace and that should give you exit code and stdout/err contents of when and command itself. Be warned, it generates a really large output.\r\n\r\nUnderstood.\r\n\r\n> Starship will try to execute your command by spawning subshell from the current parent `SHELL` ie PowerShell with `cmd.exe` used as a fallback. I guess what is happening here is that your command and when clause for some reason gets interpreted by `cmd.exe` fallback instead which choked on `$null` part thus always returning non-zero exit code.\r\n> Try setting `shell` option explicitly to `pwsh` or remove that error redirection because `when` output won't get printed anyway.\r\n\r\nI tried both suggestions and neither worked.\r\n\r\n- With shell option explicitly defined.\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[custom.git_email]\r\ncommand = \"git config user.email\"\r\nwhen = \"git rev-parse 2> $null\"\r\nshell = [\"pwsh.exe\", \"-NoProfile\", \"-Command\", \"-\"]\r\nformat = \"by [$output]($style)\"\r\nstyle = \"bright-yellow\"\r\ndisabled = false\r\n```\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/10310060/115879696-56f90080-a420-11eb-9fdf-9a98589c0074.png)\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/10310060/115879767-65471c80-a420-11eb-99b1-ff4223025139.png)\r\n\r\n- Without the error redirection.\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[custom.git_email]\r\ncommand = \"git config user.email\"\r\nwhen = \"git rev-parse\"\r\nshell = [\"pwsh.exe\", \"-NoProfile\", \"-Command\", \"-\"]\r\nformat = \"by [$output]($style)\"\r\nstyle = \"bright-yellow\"\r\ndisabled = false\r\n```\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/10310060/115879902-8a3b8f80-a420-11eb-9f1b-835c5640317e.png)\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/10310060/115879938-932c6100-a420-11eb-949f-4edabf7213a2.png)\r\n\r\nAccordingly to the logs, the command `git rev-parse` is failing as if the current directory isn't a Git repository, which makes no sense at all.\r\n\r\nAs a third option, I tried to use cmd as the shell to execute the module.\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[custom.git_email]\r\ncommand = \"git config user.email\"\r\nwhen = \"git rev-parse\"\r\nshell = [\"cmd.exe\", \"/C\"]\r\nformat = \"by [$output]($style)\"\r\nstyle = \"bright-yellow\"\r\ndisabled = false\r\n```\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/10310060/115880128-c2db6900-a420-11eb-97f7-5bcb2f1f8924.png)\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/10310060/115880159-cbcc3a80-a420-11eb-9acc-adabfe2e6f21.png)\r\n\r\nIt seems kind of broken to me. I tried `when = \"0\"` and `when = \"1\"` too, but it always executes the module despite the exit code.\r\nAnother strange behavior is that the output of the `command` is never written to the prompt.\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[custom.test_cmd]\r\ncommand = \"echo test\"\r\nwhen = \"0\"\r\nshell = [\"cmd.exe\", \"/C\"]\r\nformat = \"| CMD: [$output]($style) |\"\r\nstyle = \"bright-yellow\"\r\ndisabled = false\r\n```\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/10310060/115881924-a3ddd680-a422-11eb-9d1b-fef24363ca64.png)\r\n\r\nRunning the same in PowerShell works as expected.\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[custom.test_ps]\r\ncommand = \"echo test\"\r\nwhen = \"0\"\r\nshell = [\"pwsh.exe\", \"-NoProfile\", \"-Command\", \"-\"]\r\nformat = \"| PS: [$output]($style) |\"\r\nstyle = \"bright-yellow\"\r\ndisabled = false\r\n```\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/10310060/115883570-4f3b5b00-a424-11eb-943a-f1626eb74f78.png)\r\n\r\nIs there anything else I can do to help with the troubleshooting?",
