    "body": "@jbullers I'm experiencing the same using PowerShell 7, however I managed to find a workaround which seems to work at a decent speed\r\n\r\nI've added a `pre-prompt` to my PowerShell profile which sets my current working dir (more info here: [starship docs](https://starship.rs/advanced-config/#custom-pre-prompt-and-pre-execution-commands-in-powershell))\r\n\r\n```PowerShell\r\n# PowerShell profile\r\n\r\n# Starship prompt\r\n$ENV:STARSHIP_CONFIG = \"$HOME\\.starship\\starship.toml\"\r\n$ENV:STARSHIP_DISTRO = \"者 \"\r\n\r\nfunction Invoke-Starship-PreCommand {\r\n  $host.ui.write(\"Refreshing pwd\")\r\n  $ENV:CURRENT_DIR = $pwd.Path\r\n\r\n  $host.ui.Write(\"🚀\")\r\n  $host.ui.Write(\"$ENV:CURRENT_DIR\")\r\n}\r\n\r\n# $ENV:STARSHIP_LOG = \"trace\"\r\nInvoke-Expression (&starship init powershell)\r\n```\r\n\r\n> Note: refresh your current PowerShell profile by executing `. $PROFILE`\r\n\r\nStarship Config before (note i've replaced the output to print env var $CURRENT_DIR\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n# ~/.config/starship.toml based on https://gist.github.com/fitrh/f8c70203e3bca142d52a585e34f0248d\r\n\r\n[custom.git_host]\r\ncommand = \"\"\"\r\nURL=$(command git ls-remote --get-url 2> /dev/null)\r\n\r\nif [[ \"$URL\" =~ \"github\" ]]; then\r\n    ICON=\" \"\r\nelif [[ \"$URL\" =~ \"gitlab\" ]]; then\r\n    ICON=\" \"\r\nelif [[ \"$URL\" =~ \"bitbucket\" ]];then\r\n    ICON=\" \"\r\nelif [[ \"$URL\" =~ \"kernel\" ]];then\r\n    ICON=\" \"\r\nelif [[ \"$URL\" =~ \"archlinux\" ]];then\r\n    ICON=\" \"\r\nelif [[ \"$URL\" =~ \"gnu\" ]];then\r\n    ICON=\" \"\r\nelif [[ \"$URL\" =~ \"git\" ]];then\r\n    ICON=\" \"\r\nelse\r\n    ICON=\" \"\r\nfi\r\n\r\nfor PATTERN in \"https\" \"http\" \"git\" \"://\" \"@\"; do\r\n    [[ \"$URL\" == \"$PATTERN\"* ]] && URL=\"${URL##$PATTERN}\"\r\ndone\r\n\r\nfor PATTERN in \"/\" \".git\"; do\r\n    [[ \"$URL\" == *\"$PATTERN\" ]] && URL=\"${URL%%$PATTERN}\"\r\ndone\r\n\r\n# printf \"%s%s\" \"$ICON\" \"$URL\"\r\nprintf \"%s%s\" $CURRENT_DIR\r\n\"\"\"\r\n# command=\"$ENV:CURRENT_DIR\"\r\ndirectories = [\".git\"]\r\nwhen = 'git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree 2> /dev/null'\r\nshell = ['C:\\Program Files\\Git\\bin\\bash.exe']\r\nstyle = \"bright-yellow bold\"\r\nformat = \" [$output]($style)\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nExample output, current dir contains github repo\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6442840/159873257-c26d5542-fa98-4ae7-8f44-1840d5d217bb.png)\r\n\r\nWORKAROUND\r\n\r\nChange the config command to change to current_dir (set by pre-prompt hook) upon executing git command\r\n\r\n`URL=$(command cd $CURRENT_DIR && git ls-remote --get-url 2> /dev/null)` \r\n\r\nExample output\r\n\r\nGitlab repo\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6442840/159873908-5919bbd7-fb7f-4c07-9361-8e6acfcf0f33.png)\r\n\r\nGithub repo\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6442840/159873814-6b782fea-6381-4f8b-aaeb-881aa4ba3bb1.png)\r\n\r\nBitbucket repo\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6442840/159873853-dab348bc-ac05-475f-9036-59067cce2a6c.png)\r\n\r\nNo repo (home dir)\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6442840/159873980-08e7d5e9-fb41-4856-b05c-9d8c59ff7523.png)\r\n\r\nStarship timings\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6442840/159874277-6f68ae3b-6404-4d03-bd62-504df3997e36.png)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
